<title>FINLAND: RAUTARUUKKI MILL TO RECYCLE IRON DUST.</title>
<headline>RAUTARUUKKI MILL TO RECYCLE IRON DUST.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish steel group Rautaruukki Oy said in a statement on Monday it would invest 48 million markka in a system to reduce dust by 80 percent and recycle the iron from the dust at its Raahe Steel mill.</p>
<p>&quot;The mainly iron-containing dust will be returned as raw-material for the mill,&quot; Rautarukki said.</p>
<p>Construction of the system which would reduce dust emission by 300 tonnes per year would start next spring and the system would be taken into use at the end of next year, it said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-0-6805 0245</p>
</text>
